    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d304">

                <pb facs="0386" n="288" sameAs="frus:frus1932v04/pg288"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94 Commission/420: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland (Wilson) to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-10-05T20:00:00+01:00">October 5, 1932—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 5—4:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>21. Davis and I met McCoy in Lausanne today and had a most helpful conversation.
                    We all felt that unless something happens to change <pb facs="0387" n="289"
                        xml:id="pg289"/> the situation McCoy should not for the moment come to
                    Geneva but should hold himself available and return to this city when the
                    Commission is summoned by the Council.</p>
                <p>McCoy is deeply appreciative of the message in your 18, October 4, 4 p.m., and
                    sends his thanks and regards.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
